BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 545 Td
(1. Introduction to Memory Organization) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 1 \(Karthikeya\) | Basic Concepts & Trade-offs) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(Role of Memory in Systems:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Memory stores programs, instructions, operational data, and computation results.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Crucial subsystem directly determining processor utilization and throughput.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - CPU executes instructions at nanosecond clock speeds requiring rapid data access.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - A single memory technology cannot satisfy both maximum speed and maximum capacity.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(The Core Trade-offs & Hierarchy Strategy:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Speed vs. Cost: Faster memory technologies are substantially more expensive per bit.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Capacity vs. Speed: Larger capacity memories exhibit longer physical access latencies.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Hierarchy Strategy: Combines multiple memory technologies in a tiered structure.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Goal: Delivers nearly the speed of fastest memory with the capacity and cost of cheapest.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

endstream
