BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 545 Td
(2. Structure of Memory Hierarchy) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 1 \(Karthikeya\) | The Memory Pyramid) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(The Memory Pyramid \(Top to Bottom\):) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  1. CPU Internal Registers : Access < 1 ns | Bytes to KB | Highest cost per bit) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  2. Cache Memory \(L1, L2, L3\) : Fast SRAM bridging processor & main memory speeds) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  3. Main Memory \(RAM\) : System DRAM holding active applications and datasets \(50-100 ns\)) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  4. USB / Flash Memory : High-density solid-state intermediate storage) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  5. Magnetic Disk / Hard Disk : Secondary storage; high capacity, low cost per bit) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  6. Magnetic Tapes / Drives : Archival storage; highest capacity, lowest cost per bit) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Key Hierarchy Trends:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Downward trend: Access latency increases, capacity expands, cost per bit decreases.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

endstream
