/F1 18 Tf
50 545 Td
(3. Semiconductor RAM Memories) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 2 \(Nikhil\) | Random Access Memory \(SRAM & DRAM\)) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(Static RAM \(SRAM\):) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Storage: Built using bistable flip-flop logic circuits \(4 to 6 transistors per cell\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Speed: Very fast access times \(sub-nanosecond to few nanoseconds\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Refreshing: Does NOT require dynamic periodic refreshing while power is maintained.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Primary Application: Used exclusively for CPU internal and external Cache memory.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Dynamic RAM \(DRAM\):) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Storage: Stores bits as electrical charges in tiny capacitor-transistor pairs.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Refreshing: Charge leaks away continuously; requires periodic refreshing cycles.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Density & Cost: Extremely high bit density, simple cell layout, very low cost per bit.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Primary Application: Standard choice for computer Main Memory \(System RAM\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

endstream
