50 545 Td
(4. Read-Only Memory \(ROM\)) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 2 \(Nikhil\) | Non-Volatile Semiconductor Storage) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(ROM Characteristics & Role:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Non-Volatile: Retains program code permanently even when electrical power is disconnected.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - System Bootstrap: Holds initialization programs \(BIOS / UEFI\) and startup routines.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Embedded Firmware: Stores dedicated control routines in microcontrollers & appliances.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Normal Operation: Standard CPU operation is strictly read-only during execution.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Evolution & Types of ROM:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Mask ROM: Hardwired during fabrication; cannot be modified or updated.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - PROM: Shipped blank and electrically programmed once using fuse links.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - EPROM: Erased by exposing chip die to ultraviolet \(UV\) light.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - EEPROM: Electrically Erasable PROM; erased in-circuit via electrical signals byte-by-byte.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Flash Memory: High-density EEPROM variation erasable in large sector blocks.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

endstream
