BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 545 Td
(5. Cache Memory Architecture) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 3 \(Teja\) | High-Speed Buffer & Multi-Level Cache) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(Principles of Cache Operation:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Buffer Role: Small, ultra-fast memory placed directly between CPU execution units & DRAM.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Temporal Locality: Recently accessed items are likely to be accessed again in near future.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Spatial Locality: Items stored near recently accessed items are likely to be accessed soon.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Transparency: Operates automatically in hardware without programmer management.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Multi-Level Cache Organization:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - L1 Cache: Integrated inside CPU core; smallest \(32-64 KB\), fastest \(sub-nanosecond\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - L2 Cache: Dedicated per-core buffer; larger \(256 KB-1 MB\), slightly slower access.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - L3 Cache: Shared across all processor cores; high capacity \(8-64 MB\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Access Flow: CPU checks L1 -> L2 -> L3 -> falls back to DRAM only on cache miss.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

endstream
endobj
