BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 545 Td
(6. Cache Performance Considerations) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 3 \(Teja\) | Metrics & Access Time Analysis) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(Key Performance Metrics:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Cache Hit: Requested memory word is found directly within cache buffer.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Cache Miss: Requested word is not present, requiring retrieval from main memory.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Hit Ratio \(h\): Fraction of memory references satisfied by cache: \(Hits\) / \(Total Accesses\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Miss Ratio: Complement of hit ratio, equal to \(1 - Hit Ratio\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Miss Penalty: Extra latency required to fetch the required block from DRAM into cache.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Performance Analysis & Average Memory Access Time \(AMAT\):) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Typical Hit Ratio: 90% - 95% hit ratio drastically lowers effective memory latency.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Formula: AMAT = Hit Time + \(Miss Rate * Miss Penalty\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - High hit rates ensure CPU rarely experiences the full DRAM access delay.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

endstream
endobj
