/F1 18 Tf
50 545 Td
(7. Virtual Memory Architecture) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 4 \(Srinivas\) | Address Translation & Paging) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(Concept & Hardware Support:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Logical Address Space: Grants running programs an illusion of large, contiguous memory.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Overcoming Limits: Programs can run even if they exceed physical RAM size.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Memory Management Unit \(MMU\): Hardware component performing fast address translation.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Decoupling: Decouples user logical addresses from actual physical memory locations.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Paging & Page Fault Mechanism:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Pages & Frames: Virtual memory divided into pages; physical RAM into page frames.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Page Table: Maps process virtual pages to corresponding physical RAM frames.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Page Fault: Triggered when an active instruction references a page not currently in RAM.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Demand Paging: OS retrieves required page from secondary storage into free RAM frame.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Replacement Policy: Replaces inactive pages \(using LRU or FIFO\) when memory is full.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

endstream
