(8. Memory Management Requirements) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 4 \(Srinivas\) | Core Operating System Functions) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(Core Hardware and OS Functions:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Relocation: Dynamic address translation allowing programs to be loaded anywhere in RAM.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Protection: Prevents processes from unauthorized access to other memory areas.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Base & Limit Registers: Enforce hardware protection boundaries.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Sharing: Allows cooperating processes to access common code safely \(shared DLLs\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Logical Organization: Structures memory into logical modules, procedures, and arrays.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Physical Organization: Coordinates transparent flow between volatile RAM & secondary disk.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Maximizes multitasking throughput and system stability.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
ET

