(Role in Memory Hierarchy:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Permanent Repository: Non-volatile storage for OS kernel, applications, and user files.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Massive Capacity: Provides hundreds of gigabytes to several terabytes of storage volume.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Lowest Cost per Bit: Highly economical compared to semiconductor SRAM and DRAM.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Virtual Memory Backing: Serves as swap space holding inactive pages displaced from RAM.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Storage Media Technologies:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Solid State Drives \(SSD\): NAND flash memory; no moving parts, high IOPS, fast random access.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Hard Disk Drives \(HDD\): Magnetic platters with mechanical arms; high capacity, economical.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Removable & Optical Media: USB flash drives and optical discs \(CD/DVD/Blu-ray\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
