50 545 Td
(10. Comparison of Memory Levels) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -22 Td
(Presented by: Member 5 \(Manohar\) | Quantitative Summary Across Hierarchy) Tj
ET
50 508 m 742 508 l S
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
50 482 Td
(Quantitative Comparison Matrix:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - CPU Registers : CMOS Flip-Flops | < 1 ns | Bytes to KB | Highest Cost/Bit) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Cache Memory : Static RAM \(SRAM\) | 1 - 10 ns | KB to MB | Very High Cost/Bit) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Main Memory : Dynamic RAM \(DRAM\) | 50 - 100 ns | 8 - 64 GB | Moderate Cost/Bit) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Secondary Storage : SSD Flash / HDD Magnetic | Micro-ms | 512GB - 4TB | Lowest Cost/Bit) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
(Key Architectural Law on Memory Trade-offs:) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - As we move downward: Access time increases by orders of magnitude,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(    capacity expands dramatically, and cost per bit plummets.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(  - Ensures high-speed execution without prohibitive semiconductor manufacturing costs.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 8.5 Tf
0 -25 Td
(Digital Logic and Computer Organization -- JNTUK R23 DLCO Portal -- Team Seminar Deck) Tj
